  "footnote": "Complete 60 approved credits in chemistry and related subjects (57 for the class of 2027), including core courses and 8 laboratory credits beyond general chemistry. Place electives in Additional Space: CHEM courses at 4000 or above qualify; other-department electives require the department list, absent from this saved page. The credit check recognizes listed core/laboratory courses and CHEM 4000+; approved external electives and AP substitutions require manual verification. At most 4 credits of independent research (CHEM 4210, CHEM 4330, CHEM 4430, CHEM 4610, CHEM 4770) may count; the plan-wide check cannot cap research credits. A passing grade is required for major credit; admission normally expects C or better in introductory chemistry, CHEM 3570 or CHEM 3590, MATH 1110, and PHYS 2207 or PHYS 1112, with departmental exceptions. Standard and accelerated pathways are suggested schedules, not required concentrations. Optional Honors in Chemistry requires the honors curriculum, CHEM 3570 and CHEM 3580 or CHEM 3590 and CHEM 3600, CHEM 3890 and CHEM 3900, CHEM 3010, CHEM 3020, CHEM 3030, CHEM 4980, and a chemistry GPA of at least 3.3 at conferral. Honors seminar admission requires departmental approval; the chemistry GPA uses Cornell letter-graded CHEM courses at 2000 or above. AP chemistry credit may replace appropriate core courses. FWS courses cannot count toward the major; ENGL 2860 or ENGL 2880 used for FWS also cannot count. College residency and language exceptions require manual verification.",
